# /etc/cron.d/radar-live-backup  (copy this file there; format: min hour dom mon dow USER command)
# Nightly consistent copy of the database (SQLite VACUUM INTO, safe while radar-db runs). Each run writes
# /var/backups/radar-live/radar-<UTC timestamp>.db (mode 0600, never overwriting), verifies it with
# quick_check, and only then deletes the oldest radar-*.db files beyond the newest 14. A failed
# verification keeps all older backups. install.sh creates /var/backups/radar-live.
# Restore: see deploy/README-xubuntu.md, section 6 (Backups, restore and data safety).
17 3 * * * radar /usr/local/bin/radar-db backup --db-path /var/lib/radar-live/radar-live.db --keep 14 /var/backups/radar-live
# Key manager backup (runs as root: the vault is not readable by the service user). radar-keys-backup (installed by
# install.sh) copies keyring.json and keyvault.bin to /var/backups/radar-live/keys (root only, 0700) and keeps the newest 14.
# It NEVER copies the sealing key keyvault.key: restoring the vault needs the backup AND the original
# /var/lib/radar-keys/vault/keyvault.key (docs/keys.md).
27 3 * * * root /usr/local/sbin/radar-keys-backup
